ethercat (1.6.9+quickop1~pre6) trixie; urgency=medium

  * master: define EC_SKIP_SDO_DICT=1 and gate the master-FSM
    "fetch SDO dictionary" block behind it. The dictionary readout
    runs once per CoE slave as soon as the slave hits PREOP and
    monopolises the master FSM (and its fsm_datagram) for the whole
    transfer, which starves slave configuration and delays the
    PREOP->SAFEOP->OP path. Introspection tools (ethercat sdos) are
    the only user of this data and can request it explicitly, so
    skipping the automatic fetch is safe for I/O. This matches the
    Synapticon sncn13 build that reaches OP in ~5 s.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Wed, 22 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000

ethercat (1.6.9+quickop1~pre5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * dkms: build native Ethernet drivers alongside ec_master and
    ec_generic: ec_igc, ec_igb, ec_r8169, ec_genet, ec_e1000,
    ec_e1000e. Users can now pick any of these in DEVICE_MODULES.
  * ethercatctl stop: unload every loaded ec_* device module first,
    then ec_master, even if DEVICE_MODULES drifted between start and
    stop. Fixes "Module ec_master is in use by: ec_generic" when
    shutting the service down.
  * rules: switch userspace build to --disable-kernel and skip
    linux-headers from Build-Depends; kernel modules are built on
    the user's box via DKMS so no kernel build is needed in CI.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Wed, 22 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000

ethercat (1.6.9+quickop1~pre4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * dkms: also drop the bogus top-level Module.symvers entry from
    KBUILD_EXTRA_SYMBOLS. Kernel modpost refused to proceed when the
    referenced file did not exist, breaking ec_generic autoinstall.
  * packaging: loosen ethercat-master's dependency on libethercat to
    (>= ${source:Upstream-Version}) so upgrading between pre-releases
    or mixing +quickopN builds no longer blocks installation.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Tue, 21 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000

ethercat (1.6.9+quickop1~pre3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * dkms: fix "Is a directory" modpost failure when building
    ec_generic. devices/Kbuild.in references $(LINUX_SYMVERS) but the
    variable is never defined, so KBUILD_EXTRA_SYMBOLS pointed at the
    build tree root. Hard-wire it to Module.symvers in debian/rules
    before snapshotting the DKMS source tree.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Tue, 21 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000

ethercat (1.6.9+quickop1~pre2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Rework package split to mirror the openSUSE release layout:
    libethercat (runtime + dev files), ethercat-master (tools and
    service), ethercat-dkms (kernel module source).

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Tue, 21 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000

ethercat (1.6.9+quickop1~pre1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Quick-OP variant of IgH EtherCAT Master 1.6.9 (stable-1.6).
  * Set EC_WAIT_SDO_DICT=0 to remove the 3s wait after slave PREOP
    before SDO dictionary fetch, yielding markedly faster PREOP -> OP
    transitions. Credit: Synapticon fork of IgH EtherCAT Master
    (https://github.com/synapticon/Etherlab_EtherCAT_Master),
    commit 22b92ee ("Reduce waiting period for SDOs").
  * Debian packaging for Debian trixie; layout mirrors the openSUSE
    RPM spec. GitHub Actions CI builds .deb artifacts and publishes
    a GitHub release on tag.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Tue, 21 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
